@startuml
title Seriput server connection lifecycle

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "OPEN" as Open
state "CLOSING" as Closing
state "CLOSED" as Closed

[*] --> Open : SeriputConnection constructed\nThread: server

Open --> Closing : Peer closes connection (read returns -1)\nThread: server
Open --> Closing : Read fails with IOException\nThread: server
Open --> Closing : Write fails with IOException\nThread: server
Open --> Closing : Server shutdown begins\nThread: server

Closing --> Closed : Selection key cancelled, worker interrupted,\nchannel closed, and cleanup completed\nThread: server

Closed --> [*]

note right of Open
  The per-connection virtual worker thread:
  * handles requests
  * queues responses
  * requests OP_WRITE through the pending queue
  * observes the connection state

  It does not apply a lifecycle state transition.
end note

note right of Closing
  During normal event-loop operation, maybeClose()
  performs cleanup after read() or write() changes
  the state to CLOSING.

  During server shutdown, closeConnections()
  applies both OPEN -> CLOSING and
  CLOSING -> CLOSED.
end note

legend bottom
  All lifecycle transitions are currently applied by the
  Seriput server thread named "server".
endlegend

@enduml
